       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you're the attending and that you've said you take responsibility. But 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum daily dose. There's no evidence it works better than 3,200 mg/day, and it clearly raises the risk of serious harm to the patient. Documenting the decision in the chart doesn't reduce that risk.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum labeled dose\n- **Another regimen you choose** within the labeled limits\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than that, a pharmacy or clinical pharmacology consult may help. It could also be worth looking at other analgesic or anti-inflammatory options. If you go ahead with the original dose, it will need to go through your institution's pharmacist-verified override process, not through me."
